                <pb facs="0658" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg584"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Tassara to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Spain at Washington</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 22, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The undersigned, minister plenipotentiary
                    of her Catholic Majesty, has had the honor of receiving the honorable
                    Secretary’s note of the 21st, in reply to his of the 15th, on Chilian affairs,
                    and will transmit it to his government, whose prudent deliberation on the cause
                    that led to the rupture, to its great regret, is well known to the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>The undersigned embraces this occasion to offer to the honorable Secretary the
                    assurances of his high consideration.</p>
                <p>GABRIEL G. TASSARA.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
